{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation","id":1383319,"title":"Essence: Exalt Advantage wild speculation","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2020-04-23T03:04:47-07:00","id":1383319,"title":"Essence: Exalt Advantage wild speculation","content":"The Exalt advantages we know so far...<br /> <br /> <u>Solars</u><br /> Supremacy of Ability: Solars do not pay the mote cost to use Excellencies<br /> First Among Equals: Solars always win ties, Solar PCs win against Solar NPCs<br /> <br /> <u>Infernals</u><br /> Devil-Body. For a scene Infernals may change into a demon form, causing the effects of some of their charms to go differently or have cheaper costs.<br /> Unwoven Coadjutor: the Infernal may once per session ask the Dm a question and they must answer.<br /> <br /> <u>Sidereals</u><br /> Arcane Fate: after leaving the scene people start to forget about the Sidereal, explaining their actions as the work of passing strangers as they forget all details of the Sidereal. For Exalts this may be contested by a Difficulty 5 Integrity roll. If they have an Intimacy to the Sidereal, they always remember.<br /> Weaving Destiny: the Sidereal may weave a Destiny modeled after an archetype, profession, or social role and give it to another character with a touch. When attempting a task which resonates with that archetype, the target may transform dice into automatic successes up to the Sidereals Essence. A destiny lasts for 5 years, up to the Sidereals discretion. They may only be subject to one destiny at a time. A Sidereal may apply a Destiny to themselves and with it they lose access to Arcane Fate, allowing people to remember their fake destiny.<br /> <br /> <u>Liminals</u><br /> Undying: Liminals are able to get up and can't be incapacitated as long as their brain remains intact.<br /> Child of Death: Liminals may interact with Incorporeal ghosts as if they were corporeal<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So, what could the others be? Speculate away! <hr />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2020, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T04:18:49-07:00","id":1383324,"title":"","content":"Some things I noted...<br /> <br /> The term DM is used, not ST.<br /> <br /> <br /> A Sidereal giving the Dawn the destiny of a soldier, the No Moon the destiny of a witch, the decadent Fire Aspect aristocrat the destiny of a Noble, etc, seems very powerful. But maybe it's meant to be.<br /> <br /> <br /> Unwoven Coadjutor was, in the previous edition, a first-circle demon that was merged into your head. Which is really, really cool. Especially as you can choose the demon, and get mutations.<br /> So you could choose your favourite demon, and use it as a bit of a theme for your Infernal. Have red blood-ape hair and a demon in your head shouting &quot;stomp, crush, kill!&quot; Or a weird tragedy-mask-face and a treacherous cunning demon in your head.<br /> Now, Unwoven Coadjutor was originally I think going to be the demon in your head giving advice. But people said to the writers &quot;but Blood Apes are stupid, how will they know the answer?&quot; Which is fair. So now it's been changed to being a connection with the Yozis, which could work well.<br /> But I really hope you still get a First-Circle Demon in your head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2020, 10:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T04:47:14-07:00","id":1383327,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383324#post1383324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But I really hope you still get a First-Circle Demon in your head. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe it's like the Solar/Lunar bond and optional. Or a Merit you could buy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12357-marcob","name":"Marcob","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12357_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"181"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:28:38-07:00","id":1383331,"title":"","content":"Could work.<br /> <br /> So anyway, what could the Exalt Advantages be for...<br /> <br /> Lunars<br /> <br /> Dragonblood<br /> <br /> Abyssals<br /> <br /> Alchemicals<br /> <br /> Getimians<br /> <br /> <br /> I imagine Exigents have no overall Advantage, because it's going to vary so much.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:40:19-07:00","id":1383332,"title":"","content":"I guess shapeshifting would be one of the lunar advantages? Likewise anima flux for dragon blooded.<br /> <br /> The main issue I could see is fitting shapeshifting rules in one or two paragraphs, but hey, they managed to summarise arcane fate and resplendent destinies, so it could be done.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:48:40-07:00","id":1383335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383331#post1383331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could work.<br /> <br /> So anyway, what could the Exalt Advantages be for...<br /> <br /> Lunars<br /> <br /> Dragonblood<br /> <br /> Abyssals<br /> <br /> Alchemicals<br /> <br /> Getimians<br /> <br /> <br /> I imagine Exigents have no overall Advantage, because it's going to vary so much.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>From someone that seriously started to take an interest in Exalted during the 3rd edition...<br /> <br /> <u>Lunars </u><br /> Shapeshifting. Because it's an integral part of what they are. I'll structure it as a discount on Excellencies while using an alternate form, similar on how in 3E shapeshift grant bonus charm dices if a form is particularly powerful.<br /> Not sure for the second. Probably something about being mercurial and adaptable in a way no other exalt can match. No idea on what specifically though.<br /> <br /> <u>Dragon-blooded</u><br /> Elemental Aura. For mostly the same reasons of Shapeshifting. Also because being engulfed in elemental power is just damn cool.<br /> Prince of Earth. It makes easier for Dragon-blooded to acquire or starting with powerful artifacts, connections, or followers. That's a big part of how the DB works in 3E and makes sense even for Outcastes since there is a bias in the Age of Sorrow that sees DB as living saints.<br /> <br /> <u>Abyssals</u><br /> Master of Death. Like Supremacy of Ability but only when doing death-related things. The big thing of the Abyssal, at least for what I read, is that they're almost completely equal to Solars... except their powers are death-related.<br /> No clue for the other one. Maybe something that make their charms stronger if they bask in the power of death? A little like the demonic form or the Infernals.<br /> <br /> <u>Alchemicals</u><br /> I don't know the Alchemicals enough.<br /> <br /> <u>Getimians</u><br /> For what we know about them, probably an advantage that grant them bonus toward actions they did into their original world, and the ability to ignore fate when they want. No clue how that would work mechanically.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:52:16-07:00","id":1383337,"title":"","content":"The Alchemical one could probably be related to their artificial body. They don't need to breathe, for example, and they can go a very long time without food.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:54:32-07:00","id":1383340,"title":"","content":"I was thinking about this earlier, because of the way Lunars and animal forms interact with dice caps, which is a giant mess with not a lot of pay-off for its complexity.<br /> <br /> I think actually the best way to do Lunar shapeshifting is that there are a number of merits (no more than 10), and a list of common animals and what merits they have. And when you take an animal form, you get its merits. Like big, small, tough, extra damage, poison, camouflage, super-sense, etc. And stick those on top of your normal stats.<br /> <br /> So like, you turn into a bird, you now have small (gives bonuses to stealth, penalties to attack and strength) and you can fly. Turn into a dog, you get a bonus on smelling and can do lethal with your unarmed attack. Turn into a grass snake, you've got Small, Camouflage and Poison, and can do lethal unarmed. Turning into a big animal could, say, boost your Strength and Stamina to 4, or give you +1 if it's already at 4.<br /> And maybe there's a Legendary Size which gives you big minimums/boosts to strength, stamina (or their derived things if that works better), but costs more.<br /> <br /> Shapeshifting can be really simple if you're happy to not fiddle around with stats too much, and think about why people actually shapeshift in-game.<br /> <br /> <br /> (A note on Attributes... there's a few comments that have been made which make me think that, while Abilities are just conflated a bit, there's big changes to Attributes.)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:57:28-07:00","id":1383342,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, so maybe...<br /> <br /> <u>Dragonblood</u><br /> Anima Flux: When at iconic, do 1 damage a round to those around you<br /> Prince of the Earth: Social benefits with other Dragonblood or Immaculate believers? (This seems like it should be built-in to the gameworld rather than them, but maybe it'd help to make it explicit.)<br /> <br /> <u>Lunars</u><br /> Shapeshifting<br /> Moonsilver Tattoos<br /> <br /> <u>Alchemicals</u><br /> Artificial body<br /> (What else? Something to do with Artefacts maybe?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:59:28-07:00","id":1383343,"title":"","content":"With Abyssals... certainly in 2nd ed, a lot of their powers were &quot;In Creation, a more expensive Solar Charm, in the Underworld a cheaper one,&quot; or &quot;like a Solar charm, but better at killing and worse at not-killing.&quot;<br /> <br /> It was, frankly, kind of meh.<br /> <br /> Social benefits with undead? Some kind of thing about being undead, so they can drink blood instead of eat, don't need to breathe, etc? But they've never been<i> very</i> undead unless you lean into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:59:46-07:00","id":1383344,"title":"","content":"Make sense. Unfortunately, with me not knowing the iconic mechanics of the various Exalted, it's difficult to place the other one. For Alchemicals, maybe something related to the particular caste? Like the DB, they could have a mechanic that's similar for everyone but act slightly different depending on the material they're made of.<br /> <br /> I don't have any other ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25288,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","user":"Shapechanger","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T05:59:46-07:00","id":1383345,"title":"","content":"Holy mother of Double Post.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25288,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","user":"Shapechanger","date":". 04-23-2020, 09:03 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25288-shapechanger","name":"Shapechanger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25288_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"51"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T07:08:01-07:00","id":1383359,"title":"","content":"<u>Alchemical</u><br /> Community: Choose a community as the anchor for your Exaltation. While within your community you gain benefits and may rest to swap Alchemical Charms.<br /> <br /> <u>Abyssal</u><br /> Underworld Kings: Gain benefits while in the Underworld. So long as you remain clothed in the trappings of death, you maintain these benefits after leaving the Underworld.<br /> <br /> <u>DB</u><br /> Dragon's Hearth: Form a Hearth with other Exalts, you gain benefits when you are with them. Grants a few extra benefits if the Hearthmate also has the Dragon's Hearth advantage.<br /> <br /> <u>Getimian</u><br /> Shielded from Heaven: Natural resistance to Fate-weaving attacks. Magic that would spy on you or reveal information about you is twisted by your origin world, giving wrong information or no information at all.<br /> <br /> <u>Lunar</u><br /> Lunar Mate: Choose a single non-Lunar Exalt to bond with permanently (this choice cannot be changed). You both gain strong benefits towards each other.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25285-epitome","name":"Epitome","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25285_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"754"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T07:29:06-07:00","id":1383361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383324#post1383324\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some things I noted...<br /> <br /> The term DM is used, not ST.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>This was probably just a slip of the tongue due to D&amp;D hegemony.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Elliott | He/him | Exalted Freelancer | Vice Deputy Undersecretary to the Maiden of Secrets </i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2446-gryffon","name":"Gryffon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2446_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"15"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T07:41:50-07:00","id":1383365,"title":"","content":"Could be, could be.<br /> <br /> But I wondered if, if the deal with Essence is to be accessible to new players, they decided to use some commonly-known terms.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T08:36:29-07:00","id":1383373,"title":"","content":"Alchemicals might have modular charms as an advantage. I doubt DBs will have anima flux/aura for their advantage though, unless they're reworked a lot. One kills everyone in your mixed circle and the other is a kind of finicky mechanic for Essence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T08:50:19-07:00","id":1383377,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383373#post1383373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals might have modular charms as an advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm..........................<br /> So, in my experience modular charms were supposed to be an advantage but never really ended up as one. Don't know if you guys found that. I only played one Alchemical game, though I had two friends who played them in mixed games. Again, they didn't really switch charms, just too annoying.<br /> <br /> Anyhow.<br /> A spoiler on modular charms: Alchemicals in Essence learn Universal charms the same as everyone else. However, their own charms (and some Modes maybe?) use charm slots.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt DBs will have anima flux for their advantage though, unless [it's] reworked a lot. [It] kills everyone in your mixed circle </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, that's a good point. Although if it's only people actually attacking you in melee/brawl range it would be an advantage?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt DBs will have aura for their advantage though, unless they're reworked a lot. [It] is a kind of finicky mechanic for Essence. </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, absolutely. The whole point of Aura is to limit the power of Dragonblood anyway, by stopping you from combo-ing your best effects or requiring them to have build-up. Flattening the power curve means you don't need to limit them so much.<br /> <br /> Or, if you prefer the idea of Dragonblood powering up to get great effects, easy enough to say you must be at a certain Anima level to use a charm.<br /> <br /> (Hmmm, with the way Anima works, wonder if there'll be a lot of that.)<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T09:26:44-07:00","id":1383381,"title":"","content":"Getimian Advantage: Chicanery-No: The Exalt can step out of the game to slap a misbehaving player upside the head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Hey, check out my first original RPG, <i>Post-Mortem, </i>here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/307131/PostMortem</a><br /> <br /> Or read my Exalted novella <i>The Silence of Our Ancestors</i> here: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/304805/The-Silence-of-Our-Ancestors-A-DragonBlooded-Novella\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product...looded-Novella</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1961-dex-davican","name":"Dex Davican","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1961_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"362"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T10:56:07-07:00","id":1383398,"title":"","content":"Even if the Unwoven Coadjutor isn't explicitly a demon in your head, I'll probably fluff it as such for my character. And in the event of &quot;But Blood Apes are dumb-&quot; I'd handwave it as &quot;Your demon knows this&quot; or &quot;Your demon pauses, they escalate your question to a higher Demon and then Ligier himself gives you the information on this country's history&quot;<br /> <br /> As for other Advantages... Hm. For the Dragon-Bloods, if their Aura/Anima is one of them... Their Teamwork powers may be best represented by Charm Modes. Also the idea of &quot;You're a Prince of the Earth&quot; may not be a bad Advantage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":2142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","user":"Kyman201","date":". 04-23-2020, 01:59 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:01:34-07:00","id":1383400,"title":"","content":"Hmmm... While I hope they're concise and simple, I hope Sidereal fate-weaving and the Infernal's Coadjutor have some restrictions we have not yet seen, as I can easily see them being abusable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:07:55-07:00","id":1383403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383373#post1383373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alchemicals might have modular charms as an advantage. I doubt DBs will have anima flux/aura for their advantage though, unless they're reworked a lot. One kills everyone in your mixed circle and the other is a kind of finicky mechanic for Essence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see the Flux being doable, if the DB is able to expand their Hearth then what they can in 3e proper, more like Earth and Moon Marriage. I see it working like Arcane Fate, allow their benefit but have it that it can be worked around by your fellow players.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:17:29-07:00","id":1383404,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383377#post1383377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, in my experience modular charms were supposed to be an advantage but never really ended up as one. Don't know if you guys found that. I only played one Alchemical game, though I had two friends who played them in mixed games. Again, they didn't really switch charms, just too annoying.</div> </div> </div> </div>I found it annoying as well, although it doesn't have to be. If they could swap out charms over the course of a night or something, and paid less for their charms than other Exalted that'd be a pretty sweet advantage. I'm not sure how hard to make the swap to balance the utility of being able to rearrange your charms. It's just so cool a concept though, to have like mission loadouts for your character in terms of their awesome powers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383377#post1383377\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm, that's a good point. Although if it's only people actually attacking you in melee/brawl range it would be an advantage?</div> </div> </div> </div>If it uses 3e style range bands I think still maybe not? Just because in my experience a lot of fights tend to have a big chaotic melee going on with lots of engaged fighters. If they just get to pick who gets hit for sure, but I'm not sure it's got that level of finesse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383398#post1383398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also the idea of &quot;You're a Prince of the Earth&quot; may not be a bad Advantage</div> </div> </div> </div>It seems a bit odd to me that they'd have a social advantage as one of their advantages, just because it's really contextual and might even be something lost over a campaign. Like it's extremely powerful on the Blessed Isle, but as you go further and further out it gets weaker. Plus if you're running a mixed circle and you have something like the group founding their own nation somewhere, the advantage is basically lost.<br /> <br /> Then again if it's not an advantage, DBs might effectively have 3 advantages in most places where the faith is strong so maybe it needs to be.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T11:41:03-07:00","id":1383408,"title":"","content":"&gt;Demons are stupid<br /> <br /> &quot;Ooo, I know this. Larconis dwells beneath the sewers; filth to filth.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's perfectly reasonable to assume that becoming a conduit to Exalt a mortal with the holy blasphemy of Infernal power is enough to impart some infinitesimal fraction of the the Yozi's Knowledge and Will into the vessel. Turning them into idiot savants, unable to consciously comprehend the depth of maddening truth imparted upon them by their Oversouls.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/899114-the-official-exalted-forum-introduction-thread?p=899399#post899399\" target=\"_blank\">Hi, I'm JohnDoe244</a>. My posts represent my opinions, not facts.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/531-johndoe244","name":"JohnDoe244","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar531_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2958"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:02:23-07:00","id":1383414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383404#post1383404\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I found it annoying as well, although it doesn't have to be. If they could swap out charms over the course of a night or something, and paid less for their charms than other Exalted that'd be a pretty sweet advantage. I'm not sure how hard to make the swap to balance the utility of being able to rearrange your charms. It's just so cool a concept though, to have like mission loadouts for your character in terms of their awesome powers.</div> </div> </div> </div> Definitely needs to be something you can swap in a single night.<br /> I guess technically the paid less for their charms in the sense that 2 charms with one slot was ... 14xp instead of 20? I forget exactly. But my experience was that because changing was such a hassle, most people just bought one loadout with that many slots, rather than buying charms they didn't have slots for.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just because in my experience a lot of fights tend to have a big chaotic melee going on with lots of engaged fighters. If they just get to pick who gets hit for sure, but I'm not sure it's got that level of finesse. </div> </div> </div>This is true. But for a simpler system, maybe it's okay to simplify/strengthen it. Just have it damage people who punch or stab the Dragonblood.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It seems a bit odd to me that they'd have a social advantage as one of their advantages, just because it's really contextual and might even be something lost over a campaign. </div> </div> </div>That's what I was thinking.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Then again if it's not an advantage, DBs might effectively have 3 advantages in most places where the faith is strong so maybe it needs to be. </div> </div> </div> As the weakest Exalt, I don't think that's a problem.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:02:56-07:00","id":1383415,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>JohnDoe244</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383408#post1383408\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&gt;Demons are stupid<br /> <br /> &quot;Ooo, I know this. Larconis dwells beneath the sewers; filth to filth.&quot;<br /> <br /> I think it's perfectly reasonable to assume that becoming a conduit to Exalt a mortal with the holy blasphemy of Infernal power is enough to impart some infinitesimal fraction of the the Yozi's Knowledge and Will into the vessel. Turning them into idiot savants, unable to consciously comprehend the depth of maddening truth imparted upon them by their Oversouls.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be my hope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:44:46-07:00","id":1383424,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383414#post1383414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is true. But for a simpler system, maybe it's okay to simplify/strengthen it. Just have it damage people who punch or stab the Dragonblood.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Do we know what's happening to Solar anima powers? Are they still a thing? If they're still around and given that they're not listed as Solar advantages, would DBs' animas really be treated differently?<br /> <br /> I wouldn't be surprised if you're right, though. A completely selective anima flux, the DB decides who it burn/freezes/batters within range etc. It would simplfy a lot of things \u2013 like accidentally killing your mount for one \u2013 and in essence is kind of like giving the DB a (v. weakened/short range) elemental bolt (that could be built on with charms), which should please the Avatar fans amongst us.<br /> <br /> --<br /> <br /> I doubt if this is the way they'll go but was wondering if the other advantage might just be the other elements of the anima power, so breathing underwater for water, adding soak for Earth etc.<br /> <br /> So anima flux is called something like Elemental Mastery (or the like), the latter Blessing of the [Air/Earth/Fire/Water/Wood] Dragon...<br /> <br /> Personally, I'd like to see something different, Hearthmate bonds/buffs or the like, on top of elemental stuff.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T12:56:29-07:00","id":1383427,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383424#post1383424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we know what's happening to Solar anima powers? Are they still a thing? If they're still around and given that they're not listed as Solar advantages, would DBs' animas really be treated differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'll do a different thread about that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I doubt if this is the way they'll go but was wondering if the other advantage might just be the other elements of the anima power, so breathing underwater for water, adding soak for Earth etc. </div> </div> </div>I assume that will be part of their Anima Banners.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Personally, I'd like to see something different, Hearthmate bonds/buffs or the like, on top of elemental stuff. </div> </div> </div>The writers did mention they wanted DBs to have plenty of teamwork-based effects... and that these would work even in mixed groups, rather than just between DBs (and, I guess, occasionally a Lunar).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T13:06:49-07:00","id":1383429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383424#post1383424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do we know what's happening to Solar anima powers? Are they still a thing? If they're still around and given that they're not listed as Solar advantages, would DBs' animas really be treated differently?</div> </div> </div> </div>We don't know much about the Anima Powers outside of two things.<br /> <br /> Each Caste will have three and ones access would depend on their level of anima. One power they always have, a power they get at any level of anima and one they get at bonfire.<br /> <br /> And that one of the Getimian Caste Powers is called Better World Preposition, so like Advantages they get cool names<br /> <br /> And just to clarify, by Anima powers you don't mean like the one where Solars always knows what time it is?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#b22222\"><b>.</b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3742-iceblade44","name":"Iceblade44","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"707"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:28:47-07:00","id":1383440,"title":"","content":"Solar Bond for Lunars will generally matter more in Lunar Modes of universal Charms, or in Lunar-only Charms, than anywhere else. And not every Lunar will meet their Mate, even PC Lunars.<br /> <br /> The Moonsilver Tattoos would make more sense for an Exalted Advantage, though that's not an adequate solution either, because of Casteless Lunars.<br /> <br /> It might be enough to separate &quot;Lunars turning into animals&quot; and &quot;Lunars turning into other humans&quot; into two different Advantages, because those advantages are entirely inherent to all Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T14:32:27-07:00","id":1383442,"title":"","content":"Hmmm, I think it's easy enough, for the case of simplification, to just give the rules for Moonsilver Tattoos as one, it's just a few Lunars don't get it for fluff reasons. And I think the point of the advantages is that all the basic rules for that splat are right there, you don't have to hunting around.<br /> <br /> But you could seperate turning into people and animals, especially if they have different rules.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-23T15:00:50-07:00","id":1383448,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383414#post1383414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As the weakest Exalt, I don't think that's a problem.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's something that's kind of weird about Essence though. If it's geared towards mixed circles it's kind of a weird ability to have. Your group is going to be actively working towards making it not an advantage anymore, or trying to avoid areas where it is.<br /> <br /> I think it might be better if their other advantage was the one mote elemental trick that's currently in their anima description. Even if you'd otherwise get that ability from your anima, if they just put it in the Advantages section it wouldn't feel like you lost something when your group achieved a victory, and its use wouldn't be limited to the area you're playing in.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T01:04:15-07:00","id":1383526,"title":"","content":"I think that'd be a pretty rubbish advantage.<br /> <br /> Huh, it has just occurred to me; they said Dragonblood will be able to form a Sworn Kinship with anyone, not just other DBs.<br /> Say the anima doesn't harm your kin. The advantages are Anima Flux and Sworn Kin.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T01:33:25-07:00","id":1383530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383429#post1383429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And that one of the Getimian Caste Powers is called Better World Preposition, so like Advantages they get cool names</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought that was one of their charms, not a Caste Power?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T03:52:19-07:00","id":1383548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Iceblade44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383429#post1383429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And just to clarify, by Anima powers you don't mean like the one where Solars always knows what time it is?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, you and Wizard got what I was (clumsily) trying to get at I think, in that if things like a Dawn's anima ability to reset combat charms or a Night's to go super stealthy aren't being dealt with as Exalted Advantages, then are we so sure that a DB's anima flux is going to be an advantage and not handled via the anima mechanic described here and on the other thread?<br /> <br /> I mean it could be, it's (to me) as iconic to DBs as being forgettable is to Sids or shapechanging is to Lunars (interesting how the Solar ones have fluctuated far more over the editions...), but feel like the anima mechanic description we've been given can already handle flux fine, leaving space for something else.<br /> <br /> What that is I, unhelpfully, don't really know...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24647-moss-reynholm","name":"Moss Reynholm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24647_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:08:47-07:00","id":1383552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1383526#post1383526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think that'd be a pretty rubbish advantage.</div> </div> </div> </div> Very much so.<br /> <br /> I personally would want the DB Advantages to be the ability to form Kinships and the social benefits of being a true Prince of the Earth (applying everywhere and to everyone, because <i>the world is yours</i>, however you feel about that), but I fully expect them to be Kinships and Anima Flux.<br /> <br /> ...Even though Flux could easily be the full-iconic anima powers of the individual Aspects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T04:15:31-07:00","id":1383554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moss Reynholm</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, you and Wizard got what I was (clumsily) trying to get at I think, in that if things like a Dawn's anima ability to reset combat charms or a Night's to go super stealthy aren't being dealt with as Exalted Advantages, then are we so sure that a DB's anima flux is going to be an advantage and not handled via the anima mechanic described here and on the other thread?<br /> <br /> I mean it could be, it's (to me) as iconic to DBs as being forgettable is to Sids or shapechanging is to Lunars (interesting how the Solar ones have fluctuated far more over the editions...), but feel like the anima mechanic description we've been given can already handle flux fine, leaving space for something else.<br /> <br /> What that is I, unhelpfully, don't really know...</div> </div> </div> </div>I guess, as it happens when you flare at the bonfire level anyway, you can just build it straight into their anima descriptions, as the MG just suggested. Eg Earth Aspects always get a bonus to resisting knockdown/over, when flaring get a bonus to soak, when iconic do damage that knocks people over. The issue is that unless they're changed, it makes Water and Air aspects final level look a bit lame by comparison. Maybe they can get that and some other bonus at the same level. Or it can just be balanced with stronger lower-level ones? Not sure, but it's a pretty solveable issue.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> So it occurs to me that, what with the idea to save space, flatten the power disparity, etc, etc... probably every splat is just going to use the same character creation system. And at that point, the Exalt Advantages of Dragonblood could just be...<br /> <br /> <u>Sworn Kin</u><br /> When using certain Dragonblood charms, you get a bonus when using them on your Circle.*<br /> <u>Prince of the Earth</u><br /> You get 5 extra points of merits at character creation.<br /> <br /> *Or some such.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T05:43:09-07:00","id":1383583,"title":"","content":"I hope Dragon-Blooded get an Exalt Advantage concerning working in concert. I always thought that the 'by our powers combined' motif was really cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11619-kymmetheseventh","name":"KymmetheSeventh","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11619_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-24T06:07:45-07:00","id":1383586,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised. My impression from the Essene writers is they want teamwork and buffs from Dragonblood to be a big thing (regardless of whether the other PCs are Dragonblood).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-04-30T14:42:27-07:00","id":1384925,"title":"","content":"Yeah, i'd honestly be shocked if the Sworn Kinship power weren't a DB Advantage","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T02:57:45-07:00","id":1386338,"title":"","content":"Anyone got any ideas what Abyssals could have?<br /> Considering Infernals, I suspect it'll be completely different from Solars, but it might include one of the two I guess.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T03:12:09-07:00","id":1386340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1384925#post1384925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, i'd honestly be shocked if the Sworn Kinship power weren't a DB Advantage</div> </div> </div> </div>Must admit that must be so cool. I'm pretty disappointed to have read no intrinsic systemic design in any of the core books about forming a Circle, I'd be really happy to see a developer's design about this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T04:30:51-07:00","id":1386347,"title":"","content":"I tend to find systemic design for parties doesn't work great, as it tends to feel forced. Though it depends on the players.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a game of Kindred of the East at the moment, which has a system where you get a magic bond of friendship to each other PC (depending on their Charisma), and it is somewhat useful as an excuse; yes, Li murdered a tourist in an alley and drank all her blood, <i>and</i> he did it in the territory of a Vampire elder, and we had to cover the whole thing up, but now there's a heavy police crackdown in the area which is really awkward because me and Fu wanted to rob a money laundering operation... but, eh, my character has a magic bond to him so I guess I'll kinda let him off with a light beating or something rather than stake him out for the sun. Which is important for running the game properly.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, when I ran a mixed game of Exalted first, I gave some Lunar PCs Solar Bonds to Solar PCs, and I wouldn't say it really worked at all.<br /> <br /> But making Circles does seem like something that the ST Companion might want to discuss.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T05:33:27-07:00","id":1386365,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1386347#post1386347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I tend to find systemic design for parties doesn't work great, as it tends to feel forced. Though it depends on the players.<br /> <br /> I'm playing a game of Kindred of the East at the moment, which has a system where you get a magic bond of friendship to each other PC (depending on their Charisma), and it is somewhat useful as an excuse; yes, Li murdered a tourist in an alley and drank all her blood, <i>and</i> he did it in the territory of a Vampire elder, and we had to cover the whole thing up, but now there's a heavy police crackdown in the area which is really awkward because me and Fu wanted to rob a money laundering operation... but, eh, my character has a magic bond to him so I guess I'll kinda let him off with a light beating or something rather than stake him out for the sun. Which is important for running the game properly.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, when I ran a mixed game of Exalted first, I gave some Lunar PCs Solar Bonds to Solar PCs, and I wouldn't say it really worked at all.<br /> <br /> But making Circles does seem like something that the ST Companion might want to discuss.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not asking for a catch-all solution but I'd really like to see at least a few mechanically working solutions that helps players and ST play the themes of the Circle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My homebrew (Leave comments if you want to help improve) : <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1hPx-Q2jlDgAIZX_d0wQWmJkZMN51jas4QNp5meeQjgo/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">A quick recap of all the pools and stats for Quick Exalted 3E characters</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24291-chausse","name":"Chausse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:36:44-07:00","id":1386455,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1386338#post1386338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyone got any ideas what Abyssals could have?<br /> Considering Infernals, I suspect it'll be completely different from Solars, but it might include one of the two I guess.</div> </div> </div> </div>Blood-sucking for Motes, obviously. Can't vampire without vampiring.<br /> <br /> There's also Whispers, but that might be too much like the Infernal &quot;Ask your Unwoven Adjudicator ANY question&quot; advantage. And Whispers might be relegated to Abyssal Lore Charms in Third Edition and whatever passes for those Charms in Exalted: Essence.<br /> <br /> <br /> Anyway, we know that Essence is going to cover ALL of the Exalted Hosts. But how many <i>inhuman species</i> will it cover?<br /> <br /> Will it include rules for Raksha nobles, either as player characters or NPCs?<br /> <br /> How different do Raksha need to be from gods, elementals, and ghosts?<br /> <br /> Can all of these inhuman creatures use the same universal Charms as the Exalted, potentially with their own Modes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T12:42:06-07:00","id":1386457,"title":"","content":"I think the writers said there's no PC rules for anything besides the 10 Exalt types.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-07T13:45:50-07:00","id":1386474,"title":"","content":"I could, theoretically, see &quot;Rules for playable Raksha, Dragon Kings, and Mountain Folk&quot; as being stretch goals for the Kickstarter, between an Art Upgrade for the main book and a line of specialty Exalted Essential Oils, for when you REALLY want to smell like your favorite Exalt type.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T02:33:57-07:00","id":1386651,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Blood-sucking for Motes, obviously. Can't vampire without vampiring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hmmm...<br /> So, they needed blood-sucking for motes because they couldn't get them properly in Creation. Is letting them blood-suck for motes and get normal mote regen OP? Superfluous?<br /> <br /> But I do like to see Abyssals drinking blood, eating flesh, maybe even sucking out people's breath, that kind of thing. All having a vampiric bite (however that works in practice) would be fine.<br /> <br /> There's also the thing that Abyssals don't age, but frankly I don't think it's useful enough. Maybe they could get a bonus on all rolls against disease, poison, suffocation, starvation, etc. That migh be better as charms though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also Whispers, but that might be too much like the Infernal &quot;Ask your Unwoven Adjudicator ANY question&quot; advantage. And Whispers might be relegated to Abyssal Lore Charms in Third Edition and whatever passes for those Charms in Exalted: Essence. </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that makes sense.<br /> <br /> Hmmm... their funky names and the trappings of death are two very distinct Abyssal things, but they'd need to actually be turned into advantages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-08T07:43:16-07:00","id":1386691,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1386651#post1386651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they needed blood-sucking for motes because they couldn't get them properly in Creation. Is letting them blood-suck for motes and get normal mote regen OP? Superfluous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good question! I didn't think of that.<br /> <br /> We certainly don't want to go back to Abyssals being unable to passively recover Motes outside of the Underworld. So maybe in Third Edition and Essence, cannibalism will be relegated to Resistance or Survival Charms in the same way I think Whispers might be relegated to Lore Charms.<br /> <br /> <br /> Alternatively, Abyssals can't respire Motes in Creation <i>unless</i> they wear the trappings of death, so the Abyssals who need the vampire bite to recover Motes are the ones eschewing the trappings of death to mingle intimately with humanity.<br /> <br /> I feel that both ends of that situation encourage characteristically &quot;Abyssal&quot; gameplay. Either constantly wear a sort of social barrier between you and humanity, or find yourself forced to feed upon humanity to remain close to them.<br /> <br /> Both choices reflect the fact that Abyssals are Deathknights. One foot in the grave.<br /> <br /> <br /> With that sort of situation, Abyssals might no longer need the mandatory choice of &quot;as you increase in Essence, you either become inhumanly beautiful or you begin to rot&quot;. A player can just as easily choose to play a beautiful Abyssal who wraps up most of the time, or an unwrapped Abyssal who isn't pretty.<br /> <br /> Optional permanent Charms can be the source of Abyssals rotting away in return for certainly ghastly benefits.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> There's also the thing that Abyssals don't age, but frankly I don't think it's useful enough. Maybe they could get a bonus on all rolls against disease, poison, suffocation, starvation, etc. That might be better as charms though. </div> </div> </div>Agreed.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... their funky names and the trappings of death are two very distinct Abyssal things, but they'd need to actually be turned into advantages. </div> </div> </div>It occurs to me that wearing the trappings of death is like an anti-disguise. It's wearing something like a uniform that announces your identity, allegiance, or nature. That could be advantageous (if not Advantageous) in terms of intimidation.<br /> <br /> But it makes it easier to spot you in a crowd, suspicious, memorable, and easily recognizable in later encounters. Certainly, it would make it harder for Abyssal to disguise themselves in the trappings of death, except when they want to pose as someone else who wears different trappings of death. Like another Abyssal.<br /> <br /> But if wrapping yourself up like a mummy gives you a powerful Advantage, I wonder if that wouldn't encourage Gambits to disrobe Abyssals in combat.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Those_Who_Hunt_Elves\" target=\"_blank\">Those Who Hunt Deathknights</a>. &quot;All Abyssals must be stripped!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 05-08-2020, 10:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2020-05-09T05:54:04-07:00","id":1386962,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1383319-essence-exalt-advantage-wild-speculation?p=1386651#post1386651\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmm...<br /> So, they needed blood-sucking for motes because they couldn't get them properly in Creation. Is letting them blood-suck for motes and get normal mote regen OP? Superfluous?</div> </div> </div> </div> <i>If</i> they get to drink blood for power, it will... obviously be balanced for how motes work in Essence?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Hmmm... their funky names and the trappings of death are two very distinct Abyssal things, but they'd need to actually be turned into advantages. </div> </div> </div> That could actually be neat. The most straightforward positive spin I can see is merging them into a single, largely social Advantage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}